            "review_title": "Review at Di Nam Bun Bo Hue",
            "review_text": "mattblack\nAdelaide92 contributions\n0\nGood Noodle Soup close to Hanoi Train Station to Sapa\nMay 2013 • Couples\nMy wife and I had a room at a Hotel opposite the train station in Hanoi for a few hours before our overnight train to Sapa. We were keen to have a meal somewhere, so wandered around to try to find something. We are reasonably adventurous, but couldn't find anything that looked appetising at first. Then a gentleman from this restaurant called us over and explained what they were serving - Hue style noodle soup. He explained that he had just opened up the restaurant and that his wife ran it during the day and he came to help out when not working in his other job. He was a very nice bloke, introduced his wife and kids and urged his kids to practice their english with us (they were shy but very good speakers).\n\nWe had a bowl of beef noodle soup each and it was very good. Simple of course, but clean and comfortable surroundings, nice owners, and good place for a cheap delicious meal before our train ride to Sapa. We couldn;t find much in this area on tripadvisor so submitted this place to be included on TA.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten September 5, 2013",
